@spec patternEditor_modal_spec  src=tests/specs/patternEditor_modal_spec.lua  loc=166  cases=4
@exercises keyQueue (kq), scratch (scratch)
@surface   kq:fill, scratch.track, kq:take
@harness   mk, reaper.GetMediaItemTake_Track, reaper.CountTrackMediaItems

# Intent
  design/fx-patterns.md P3 step d: the modal editing surface. Pins that launch
  raises the modal + sweeps on close, that the mini cmgr dispatches the editing
  subset onto the checkout (a whitelisted command edits it, an excluded chord is
  inert), and that an unconsumed Esc closes. Drives the real handleInput pass
  against a controllable imgui; no grid draw.

# Helpers
  @fn setKeys(keys, mods)  @ 38-42
      -- The mini editor runs inside the modal the fill records as owner, and claims under that
      -- name, so the queue each pass reads is filled as one. See docs/keyQueue.md § Ownership.
  @fn newModalHost()  @ 48-53
      -- Capture the open state so a test can invoke onClose the way modalHost would.
  @fn loadPE(deps)  @ 55-63
  @fn noop()  @ 79
  @fn withEditor(harness)  @ 81-86

# Cases
  @case 'launch mints a checkout and raises the modal; onClose sweeps it'  [harness]  @ 90-104
  @case 'a whitelisted key dispatches on the mini cmgr; an excluded chord is inert'  [harness]  @ 108-125
  @case 'the chord gesture is gated off the pattern surface'  [harness]  @ 129-152
  @case 'an unconsumed Esc closes the modal'  [harness]  @ 156-164

# Uses (outbound edges)
  @use call kq:fill  @ 41
  @use call scratch.track  @ 93
  @use call kq:take  @ 118,124

